    _item("ebla-archives", "ebla", "Ebla Palace G Archives", "cuneiform palace archive", "mid-3rd millennium BCE", "comparative Syrian urban context", "They document a complex Syrian court, economy, and scribal culture long before the biblical narratives were written.", "Place-name similarities or broad cultural parallels do not establish direct biblical correlations.", "Thousands of tablets and fragments from the Palace G archive at Ebla.", "Italian excavations found tablets collapsed on shelves in the palace archive rooms in the 1970s.", "Clay tablets in Sumerian and Eblaite, including lexical, administrative, and diplomatic texts.", "The archive is primary evidence for literacy and state administration in Early Bronze Syria.", "It supplies broad comparative background for Genesis's northern Syrian and Mesopotamian horizon without proving patriarchal traditions.", "c. 2400–2250 BCE", "Stratigraphy, script, and archive context", "The archive's significance is established; early popular claims about direct biblical names are not accepted as reliable evidence.", "Idlib Museum collections and excavation archives", "Sapienza University of Rome", "https://ebla-archive-archivio-ebraico.saras.uniroma1.it/", periods=["Broad / uncertain period"], dispute="interpretation_disputed"),
